@@ -0,0 +1,171 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""How many checks read git's STDOUT without ever asking whether git RAN?
+
+THE FAILURE THIS COUNTS. `git status --porcelain` outside a work tree exits 128
+and prints nothing; `git ls-files` exits 128 and prints nothing; `git log` the
+same. Empty stdout is also exactly what SUCCESS looks like when there is nothing
+to report. So a caller that reads `.stdout` and never looks at `returncode`
+cannot distinguish "git says there is nothing" from "git did not run", and its
+check silently passes. A staged panel sandbox carries no `.git`, so this is the
+ordinary environment for a reviewer, not an exotic one.
+
+THREE CONFIRMED INSTANCES PROMPTED THIS CENSUS, all found by execution:
+  * `test_measurement_survey_is_safe_2026-09-11.py` compared porcelain before
+    against after -- `'' == ''` -- and held while the tree was written to.
+  * `overstated_entries_2026-09-11.py::tracked` returned `rc == 0`, making V2's
+    headline 100.0000% where the repaired probe reads 0.0000%.
